oud`). Semblr's `ctx.modelRegistry` stores models with `provider` and `id`\n   fields. How should the string `\"glm-5.2:cloud\"` be parsed? Options:\n   - Treat the whole string as a `provider/id` and split on `/`.\n   - Treat the suffix `:cloud` as a tag, and use Ollama as the provider.\n   - Just match `id === \"glm-5.2:cloud\"` literally.\n\n   Semblr does not currently have a model-resolution helper. This should be a\n   dedicated function (`resolveModelId(mapValue: string, registry: ModelRegistry)`)\n   and be the subject of a test that verifies it picks the right entry. The spec does\n   not pin this down, so the implementer has latitude.\n\n3. **What does \"agent cycle\" mean for the switch counter?** The agent loop is one user\n   prompt → many LLM turns. The counter should probably reset on `agent_start` (i.e. per\n   user prompt). The spec says \"3 per agent cycle\" — I read \"agent cycle\" as \"agent_start\n   → agent_end window\". Worth a confirm in the PR.\n\n4. **Note injection on the first round of a session.** If the very first user prompt\n   triggers a switch (somehow), there's no prior round to attach the note to. The note\n   should be dropped in that edge case. Currently handled by the `lastRoundFileName` /\n   `injectedPhaseTransitionRounds` pattern, but worth a test.\n\n5. **Should the note be included in the round's saved JSON?** Useful for debugging and\n   for future analysis. The spec does not require it but does not forbid it. Recommend\n   including `reportedPhase` and `phaseNote` on `RoundData` as optional fields.\n\n6. **What happens if the LLM calls `semblr_report_phase` AFTER another tool has\n   already produced output in the same round?** The spec says \"store the phase + note\n   in round state\" — i.e. the last call wins. That matches the simple-storing plan\n   above. Worth a test.\n\n7. **What about mid-response phase changes?** Comment #1 explicitly says routing happens\n   only at `agent_end`. So even if the LLM calls the tool multiple times during one\n   response, only the last call's value matters and the switch happens *after* the\n   response completes. That is the simple interpretation; matches the MVP scope.\n\n8. **Idempotency of the announcement.** If `pi.setModel` succeeds but the tool was\n   already called with the same phase previously this round, should we re-announce? My\n   reading: no — only announce on the first successful switch of this round. But the\n   spec is silent.\n\n9. **What if the LLM reports a phase but the target model is the same as the\n   current model?** The spec step 6 says \"Is the target model different from the\n   current model?\" — answer: skip the switch silently, do not announce, do not\n   increment the counter. (This is the cheap \"no-op\" path.)\n\n10. **Cancellation: what if the LLM calls `semblr_report_phase` during compaction?**\n    Out of scope for MVP (compaction is cancelled by Semblr anyway), but worth noting.\n\n## 8. Summary For Reviewers\n\n- **What:** Add a `semblr_report_phase` tool that captures an LLM-self-reported\n  generation phase + free-form note, and use that to switch to a hardcoded phase→model\n  map at `agent_end`. Strict MVP — no presets, no config knobs, no TUI, no slash command.\n- **Why:** Issue #86 is a \"let's see if this works\" data-gathering experiment. The\n  project owner is deliberately constraining scope to keep the blast radius small while\n  gathering evidence.\n- **How:** New config key + env var, new state fields, new tool, new agent_end branch,\n  new context-injection section. All changes are additive and opt-in. No existing\n  behaviour changes when `routing.enabled = false` (the default).\n- **Where to start:** `lib/semblr-config.ts` (config), `lib/routing.ts` (new pure\n  helpers), `lib/state.ts` (state), `src/semblr.ts` (tool + agent_end + context).\n- **Branch:** `feature/86-multi-model-routing`\n- **Tests:** 4 test files need additions; 1 new test file (`lib/routing.test.ts`).\n- **Docs:** REA