{"type":"message","id":"3d457c73","parentId":"f8ac9f6a","timestamp":"2026-06-24T08:52:33.018Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_eRO3BLR8nT9Vu0gWcaqB6524","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Task 004: Implementation Summary\n\n**Task:** Multi-model routing — core extension changes in `src/semblr.ts` and library support\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Tool Registration (`src/semblr.ts`, line ~1515)\n\nRegistered `semblr_report_phase` tool with a Pi native tool registration via `pi.registerTool()`. The tool:\n\n- **Name:** `semblr_report_phase`\n- **Schema:** Uses TypeBox (`Type.Union` / `Type.Literal`) to restrict `phase` parameter to the six `PhaseName` values: `thinking`, `executing`, `stuck`, `reporting`, `reviewing`, `verifying`\n- **Prompt snippet:** `\"Report your current generation phase for multi-model routing\"`\n- **Tool label:** `\"Report Phase\"`\n\n### 2. Handler Logic (`src/semblr.ts`, lines ~1541-1595)\n\nThe `execute` handler implements the routing decision pipeline:\n\n1. **Disabled gate:** If `SEMBLR_CONFIG.multiModelRouting.enabled` is false, returns early with \"not enabled\" message\n2. **Store phase:** Sets `round.currentPhase` to the reported phase\n3. **Look up target:** Reads target model from `SEMBLR_CONFIG.multiModelRouting.phaseModelMap[phase]`\n4. **Null target (thinking phase):** Clears `pendingModelSwitch` to null — no switch\n5. **Idempotency check:** If `pendingModelSwitch` already equals target, skip (avoids double-counting)\n6. **Same-model check:** If the current model already matches the resolved target model ID, skip\n7. **Switch limiter:** If `round.switchCounter >= maxSwitches` (default: 3), blocks further switches\n8. **Commit pending switch:** Sets `round.pendingModelSwitch = targetModel` and increments `round.switchCounter++`\n\nResponse is always `Phase recorded: {phase}.` regardless of routing decision, keeping the tool opaque to the LLM about routing internals.\n\n### 3. Model Switching at agent_end (`src/semblr.ts`, lines ~1090-1120)\n\nThe actual `pi.setModel()` call happens at the `agent_end` lifecycle hook (round boundary):\n\n- Checks `SEMBLR_CONFIG.multiModelRouting.enabled && round.pendingModelSwitch`\n- Resolves the target model ID via `resolveModelId()` (strips `:cloud` suffix, provider = `ollama`)\n- Skips if already on target model (`ctx.model?.id === resolvedId`)\n- Looks up model object from `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, resolvedId)`\n- Falls back gracefully: notifies error if model not found or setModel fails\n- Resets `round.pendingModelSwitch = null` regardless of success/failure\n\n### 4. Stream Announcements\n\nUses `ctx.ui.notify()` for all user-facing messages:\n\n- **On successful switch:** `\"[Multi-model] Switching to {targetModel} for {phase} phase (switch {counter}/{maxSwitches})\"` (info level)\n- **On missing model:** `\"[Multi-model] Model not found in registry: {targetModel}\"` (error level)\n- **On setModel failure:** `\"[Multi-model] Failed to switch to {targetModel} for {phase} phase (no API key configured?)\"` (error level)\n\n### 5. Context Injection\n\n**`src/semblr.ts` (line 156):**\n```ts\nconst ROUTING_INSTRUCTIONS = SEMBLR_CONFIG.multiModelRouting.enabled ? buildRoutingInstructions() : null;\n```\n\nComputed once at extension load time; `null` when routing disabled.\n\n**`lib/context-format.ts` (lines ~372-410):**\n`buildRoutingInstructions()` returns a `[MULTI-MODEL ROUTING]` text block teaching the LLM the phase semantics and how to call `semblr_report_phase`. Covers all six phases with plain-English descriptions and the rule: \"report what you will do NEXT, not what you just did.\"\n\n**`lib/context-messages.ts` (line 133):**\n`ContextBlocks` interface extended with `routingInstructions: string | null` field.\n\n**`lib/context-messages.ts` (line 159):**\n`assembleContextPrefix()` injects routing instructions as a user text message after `workingMemory` and before `preamble` in the fixed-order prefix asse